[1m[38;5;231mWhich approach should the design use?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mA: login() writes (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mlogin() calls Session.setUserId() on success. One writer, enforced structurally; callers cannot forget to persist.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m B: caller writes
     [38;5;246mlogin() stays pure and returns the userId; the submit handler persists it. Best testability, but persistence [39m
     [38;5;246mbecomes caller discipline.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m C: Session.login() facade
     [38;5;246msession.js owns the auth flow and persists internally. One auth surface for future forms, at the cost of a layer [39m
     [38;5;246mbuilt for a consumer that does not exist yet.[39m
